Lane Scheduler — Code Review
I read the source files and ran the test suite + sim harness. Findings below; line refs verified.
Critical — fix first
C1. [DONE] Scheduler has no internal locks; pod-watch and cycle thread race on shared dicts
	Fixed in "Harden scheduler concurrency, watch resumption, and admission retries":
	Scheduler._lock = threading.RLock() added; cycle, submit, register_class,
	_scored_candidates, queue_rank, queue_depths, and class_scores all acquire it.
	UtilizationTracker keys pruned on read. Snapshot reads pending_count under
	_pending_lock. _dispatched accumulator removed (callers use cycle()'s return value).
C2. [DONE] Watches do not preserve resourceVersion across reconnect — silent event loss
	Fixed in same commit: watch loops store and forward resourceVersion, handle 410 Gone
	by re-listing, accept Bookmark events, and seed initial state from list_pod /
	list_node so no events are lost on first iteration.
C3. [DONE] simulate.py is broken
	Fixed in same commit: tools/simulate.py rewritten for the dynamic Lane enum;
	initialise_lanes() called before any Lane access. `python tools/simulate.py`
	runs end-to-end again.
C4. Unbounded growth in DeficitTracker._deficit and UtilizationTracker._events
	scheduler.py:273, 246 — UtilizationTracker keys are now pruned on read (done).
	DeficitTracker._deficit is still keyed by (student_id, lane) and never pruned.
	Across a multi-term deployment with thousands of students, _deficit grows without
	bound. No per-term reset hook exists.
	Remaining fix: GC DeficitTracker keys with no recent activity on CSV reload, or
	prune entries whose last-event timestamp is older than the utilization window.
C5. [DONE] _handle_pod_event ignores DELETED
	Fixed in same commit: DELETED events now call Scheduler.remove_job, clearing the
	job from _queues so orphan Jobs no longer linger after force-delete.
High
H1. [DONE] Documentation drift — test counts and lane labels
	Fixed in same commit: README.md and CLAUDE.md test counts updated to 219;
	manifests.yaml header comments corrected to reference gpu-class labels
	(not the stale dsmlp/gpu-pool=interactive/batch).
H2. Manifest image: <ghcr.io/agt/lane-scheduler:latest>, no probes, no securityContext
	manifests.yaml:104 still uses :latest. No livenessProbe/readinessProbe added.
	No securityContext (runAsNonRoot, readOnlyRootFilesystem, allowPrivilegeEscalation:
	false, seccompProfile). replicas: 1 with no PDB, no leader election.
	Still needs: pinned image digest or semver tag; liveness/readiness probes;
	securityContext block; PodDisruptionBudget.
H3. CronJob template is non-functional as written
	manifests.yaml:162-170 — the curl fetch is still commented out; the kubectl
	create configmap line references /tmp/courses.csv which no one populates.
	Deploying as-is silently does nothing every morning.
	Still needs: either a real fetch command (uncommented curl) or an explicit
	`exit 1` so the job fails loudly instead of silently succeeding.
H4. [DONE] cycle() and _admit_pod retry semantics
	Fixed in same commit: per-pod exponential backoff capped at 5 min,
	_MAX_ADMIT_ATTEMPTS=5. Pods in backoff are skipped by the cycle thread.
	On give-up, the Job and _pending entry are dropped and a Warning Event is emitted.
H5. Patch payload is a JSON-merge patch but called via patch_namespaced_pod without content-type
	Not re-verified post-refactor. Confirm that strategic-merge on spec.tolerations
	correctly appends rather than replaces the array, and add a test asserting that
	pre-existing tolerations survive admission.
H6. Web server: no auth, binds 0.0.0.0
	web/server.py still exposes queue contents and student namespace counts with
	no auth and no TLS. Either bind to 127.0.0.1 and require port-forward, or
	front with auth middleware.
H7. [DONE] epsilon, t_half, mean_pct/std_pct not validated
	Fixed in same commit: SchedulerConfig.__post_init__ validates alpha >= 0
	and all other config fields > 0, preventing inf scores and zero-division crashes.
H8. Snapshot reads aren't atomic across _pending / _running / scheduler queues
	web/snapshot.py — pending_count now read under _pending_lock (done). Full
	atomicity across _pending / _running / scheduler queues still not guaranteed;
	a pod transitioning between states across the three separate lock acquisitions
	can appear in both halves or neither.
	Remaining fix: acquire all locks in a fixed order for the full snapshot, or
	build it inside the cycle thread and publish atomically.
Medium
M1. [DONE] _running_ctx leaks on missed completion
	Fixed in same commit: _running_ctx tuples carry a ctx_created timestamp; the
	cycle thread sweeps entries older than 24 h whose uid is no longer in _running.
M2. Pod-UID as job id, but jobs survive in _queues across pod recreation
	pod_translator.py:139-169 — if _dequeue misses a deletion, a recreated pod
	with a new UID sits alongside the dead Job in the same student bucket. Deficit
	accounting won't notice and keeps accruing. No change made yet.
M3. [DONE] Batch milestone math freezes after first estimate
	Fixed in same commit: event_publisher re-anchors milestones when the median
	wait estimate grows more than 2x the original anchor (never shrinks).
M4. CSV reload is all-or-nothing but silently accepts a shrunken file
	course_registry.py — no sanity check on registry size after reload. A truncated
	export silently replaces the full registry. Still needs a guard (e.g., refuse
	to replace if new size < 50% of old) and a log line when the count changes.
M5. [DONE] lane_for_gpu_class silently falls back
	Fixed across two commits: lane_for_gpu_class gains strict=True returning None
	for unknown classes; pods with unknown gpu-class are ignored (not enqueued) and
	receive a Warning Kubernetes event (reason: UnknownGpuClass). NodeCapacityTracker
	also uses strict lookup and excludes nodes with unmanaged gpu-class labels.
M6. [DONE] Graceful shutdown doesn't stop in-flight watches
	Fixed in same commit: watch handles stored on the controller; stop() calls
	w.stop() on each handle to interrupt blocking streams; threads joined with a
	timeout on SIGTERM.
M7. [DONE] No SIGINT handler
	Fixed in same commit: SIGINT handler registered alongside SIGTERM so Ctrl-C
	also triggers graceful shutdown and syncs residency stats.
Low
	•	[DONE] Dockerfile pins python:3.11.10-slim and uses a single editable install
	  (pyproject.toml drives all dependencies; kubernetes~=36.0 pinned).
	•	[DONE] _dispatched accumulator removed — no longer a slow leak.
	•	No HEALTHCHECK in Dockerfile, no /healthz in the web server.
	•	Tests still missing for: malformed pods, watch reconnection, CSV truncation,
	  NaN in residency profile. (Concurrent submit/cycle, config validation,
	  remove_job, DELETE→queue, admission backoff now covered — 219 passing.)
	•	Logging: pod names still logged unsanitized; long namespaces produce noisy lines.
Top-5 remaining
	1.	Finish C4: prune DeficitTracker._deficit on CSV reload to prevent multi-term unbounded growth.
	2.	Fix H2: pin image to a semver/digest tag; add liveness/readiness probes and securityContext to the Deployment.
	3.	Fix H3: uncomment or replace the CronJob fetch command so it fails loudly when /tmp/courses.csv is absent.
	4.	Fix H8 + M2: make snapshot reads fully atomic; handle pod-UID reuse so dead Jobs don't survive in student buckets.
	5.	Fix M4: add CSV-size sanity check to course_registry.py to reject suspiciously shrunken registrar exports.
Documentation
	•	README.md now has two sections covering overlapping ground: the prose Goals section
	  (lines ~7–19) and the new Scheduling Model section added for academic audiences. A human
	  should review both for consistency of framing and remove any redundancy — in particular,
	  the Goals bullets and the Scheduling Model opening sentence describe the same fairness
	  problem from different angles and may benefit from consolidation or a clearer transition.
